# Start the Wi-Fi supplicant at boot, independent of the app.
#
# Buildroot's own preset (50-wpa_supplicant.preset) says
# "disable wpa_supplicant@.service", and the rootfs step runs
# `systemctl preset-all`, which deletes any wants link that contradicts a
# preset. So the instance has to be enabled HERE, not with a symlink in
# post-build or the overlay: presets are read in lexical order and the
# first match wins, so 40- beats Buildroot's 50-.
#
# Without this, nothing in the image starts the supplicant; only the app
# does (ensure_supplicant in revokyte). A device whose app never starts -
# a display that does not come up, a crash at import - then has no network
# at all, which is exactly when it is needed for diagnosis and for the OTA
# that fixes it. (wifi-setup.service used to pull the instance in with
# Wants=; it went away with boot-partition Wi-Fi provisioning.)
enable wpa_supplicant@.service wlan0
